A||||2||Tweek||Steering Column Compatibility||||1||
Z||000000||Tweek||06-13-2001||06:17 PM||||Greetings All.<P>My steering column is quite loose and wobbly. As I don't have the tools required to fix it (the loose torx botls), I would rather replace it. The junkuyards in my area will sell me a steering column plus steerin wheel for like $20-$25. But after checking many of them, none of them have keys, and many are missing the stalk. <P>Soooo....   What other vehicles can I get one from? Anyone have any ideas? Should I just look for one thats similar with the same options as mine? Or maybe there are distinct differences..   Thanks for your input.||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||06-13-2001||07:14 PM||||Any good yard should have a parts book that will tell you what other cars have these columns. Many small GM cars will probably have one. These columns are by no means unique to Fiero.<P>You can change the bad locks.... you'll have to pull the steering wheel and lock plate. It's held by a screw under there... There's an article in my cave that might help. It has links to Oliver's picture page for the column.||||reg||1
Z||000002||cadaver||06-14-2001||12:45 AM||||If you have to remove the steering wheel and lock plate to get to the lock cylinder to swap it out why not just fix the column. You will be alreadt there.<BR>You can get the tools on loan from most decent parts stores or by cheap one for around $20 for both. The steering wheel puller and the lock plate tool.||||reg||1
